repository-code: 'https://github.com/othmani-samir-gh/leo-metric-ns3-reproduction'
abstract: >-
  An independent ns-3 reconstruction of the Low Energy and Overhead (LEO)
  wireless-sensor-network routing metric, with hop-count and ZigBee LQI
  comparators. Version 1.1.0 requalifies the simulator through regression
  testing, deterministic RNG streams, frozen experiment provenance, complete
  raw-data regeneration, paired statistical reanalysis, and checksum-bound
  figures and claims. In the source-constrained static non-interference
  analysis, LEO reduces timeout and no-route outcomes versus hop-count, while
  its energy effect depends on the relay cap; LEO uses more energy than the
  operational LQI comparator in the tested primary strata. Mobility and
  reconstruction-parameter studies are reported separately as exploratory
  or sensitivity analyses. The repository does not claim exact replay of the
  original authors' unpublished simulator code.
keywords:
  - wireless sensor networks
  - routing metrics
  - ns-3
  - energy-efficient routing
  - reproducibility
  - simulation validation
  - node mobility
